    {
      "number": "330-331",
      "title": "The Spacious Firmament on High",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/The-Spacious-Firmament-on-High.pdf",
      "audioUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-audio/cc_330-331.mid",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "The spacious firmament on high,\nwith all the blue ethereal sky,\nand spangled heavens, a shining frame,\ntheir great Original proclaim.\nThe unwearied sun from day to day\ndoes his Creator's power display,\nand publishes to every land\nthe work of an almighty hand."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Soon as the evening shades prevail\nthe moon takes up the wondrous tale,\nand nightly to the listening earth\nrepeats the story of her birth;\nwhilst all the stars that round her burn,\nand all the planets in their turn,\nconfirm the tidings, as they roll,\nand spread the truth from pole to pole."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "What though in solemn silence all\nmove round the dark terrestrial ball;\nwhat though nor real voice nor sound\namid their radiant orbs be found;\nin reason's ear they all rejoice,\nand utter forth a glorious voice,\nfor ever singing as they shine,\n'The hand that made us is divine.'\nSource:\nAncient and Modern: hymns and songs for refreshing worship #550"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
