        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Jesus, the very thought of thee\nwith sweetness fills the breast;\nbut sweeter far thy face to see,\nand in thy presence rest."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "O hope of every contrite heart,\nO joy of all the meek,\nto those who fall, how kind thou art!\nHow good to those who seek!"
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "But what to those who find? Ah, this\nnor tongue nor pen can show;\nthe love of Jesus, what it is,\nnone but his loved ones know."
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Jesus, our only joy be thou,\nas thou our prize wilt be;\nJesus, be thou our glory now,\nand through eternity."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "362-363",
      "title": "Lord, Thee I Love with All My Heart",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/Lord-Thee-I-Love-with-All-My-Heart.pdf",
      "audioUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-audio/cc_362-363.mp3",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "The King of love my shepherd is,\nwhose goodness faileth never.\nI nothing lack if I am his,\nand he is mine forever."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Where streams of living water flow,\nmy ransomed soul he leadeth;\nand where the verdant pastures grow,\nwith food celestial feedeth."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Perverse and foolish, oft I strayed,\nbut yet in love he sought me;\nand on his shoulder gently laid,\nand home, rejoicing, brought me."
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "In death's dark vale I fear no ill,\nwith thee, dear Lord, beside me;\nthy rod and staff my comfort still,\nthy cross before to guide me."
        },
        {
          "number": 5,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Thou spreadst a table in my sight;\nthy unction grace bestoweth;\nand oh, what transport of delight\nfrom thy pure chalice floweth!"
        },
        {
          "number": 6,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "And so through all the length of days,\nthy goodness faileth never;\nGood Shepherd, may I sing thy praise\nwithin thy house forever."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "364",
      "title": "O God of Earth and Altar",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/O-God-of-Earth-and-Altar.pdf",
      "audioUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kVqKDRR8aEA",
      "notes": "Video: https://youtu.be/O5axEKP6ZCk?si=SBukkXMtMYa9EY50",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Spirit of God, who dwells within my heart,\nwean it from sin, through all its pulses move.\nStoop to my weakness, mighty as you are,\nand make me love you as I ought to love."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "I ask no dream, no prophet ecstasies,\nno sudden rending of the veil of clay,\nno angel visitant, no opening skies;\nbut take the dimness of my soul away."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Did you not bid us love you, God and King,\nlove you with all our heart and strength and mind?\nI see the cross— there teach my heart to cling.\nO let me seek you and O let me find!"
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Teach me to feel that you are always nigh;\nteach me the struggles of the soul to bear,\nto check the rising doubt, the rebel sigh;\nteach me the patience of unceasing prayer."
        },
        {
          "number": 5,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Teach me to love you as your angels love,\none holy passion filling all my frame:\nthe fullness of the heaven-descended Dove;\nmy heart an altar, and your love the flame."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "364-365",
      "title": "May God Bestow on Us His Grace",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/May-God-Bestow-on-Us-His-Grace.pdf",
      "audioUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-audio/cc_364-365.mid",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Marvelous grace of our loving Lord,\ngrace that exceeds our sin and our guilt,\nyonder on Calvary's mount out-poured,\nthere where the blood of the Lamb was spilt."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": true,
          "text": "Grace, grace, God's grace,\ngrace that will pardon and cleanse within;\nGrace, grace, God's grace,\ngrace that is greater than all our sin."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Sin and despair like the sea waves cold,\nthreaten the soul with infinite loss,\nGrace that is greater, yes, grace untold,\npoints to the refuge, the mighty cross. [Refrain]"
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Dark is the stain that we cannot hide,\nwhat can avail to wash it away?\nLook! there is flowing a crimson tide;\nwhiter than snow you may be today. [Refrain]"
        },
        {
          "number": 5,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Marvelous, infinite, matchless grace,\nfreely bestowed on all who believe;\nall who are longing to see His face,\nwill you this moment His grace receive? [Refrain]\nSource:\nOur Great Redeemer's Praise #558"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "368",
      "title": "Lord, Keep Us Steadfast in Thy Word",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/Lord-Keep-Us-Steadfast-in-Thy-Word.pdf",
      "audioUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-audio/Lord-Keep-us-Steadfast-386.mp3",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Lord, keep us steadfast in your Word;\ncurb those who by deceit or sword\nwould seek to overthrow your Son\nand to destroy what he has done."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Lord Jesus Christ, your pow'r make known,\nfor you are Lord of lords alone;\ndefend your Christendom that we\nmay sing your praise eternally."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "O Comforter of priceless worth,\nsend peace and unity on earth;\nsupport us in our final strife\nand lead us out of death to life.\nSource:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "370-371",
      "title": "O Let My Name Engraven Stand",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/O-Let-My-Name-Engraven-Stand.pdf",
      "audioUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-audio/cc_370-371.mid",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Who is this fair one in distress,\nThat travels from this wilderness;\nAnd, pressed with sorrows and with sins,\nOn her beloved Lord she leans?"
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "This is the spouse of Christ our God,\nBought with the treasures of his blood;\nAnd her request and her complaint\nIs but the voice of every saint:"
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "“O let my name engraven stand\nBoth on thy heart and on thy hand;\nSeal me upon thy arm, and wear\nThat pledge of love for ever there."
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "“Stronger than death thy love is known,\nWhich floods of wrath can never drown;\nAnd hell and earth in vain combine,\nTo quench a fire so much divine."
        },
        {
          "number": 5,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "“But I am jealous of my heart,\nLest it should once from thee depart;\nThen let thy name be well impressed,\nAs a fair signet, on my breast."
        },
        {
          "number": 6,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "“Till thou hast brought me to thy home,\nWhere fears and doubts can never come,\nThy countenance let me often see,\nAnd often thou shalt hear from me.”\nSource:\nA Selection of Hymns for Public Worship. In four parts (10th ed.) (Gadsby's Hymns) #92"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "372a",
      "title": "Lord, Teach Us How to Pray Aright",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/Lord-Teach-Us-How-to-Pray-Aright.pdf",
      "audioUrl": "https://hymnary.org/media/fetch/205803/public%3A//hymnary/media/ELW2006/ELW745_Lord%2C_Teach_Us_How_to_Pray_Aright.mp3",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "O love, how deep, how broad, how high!\n\r\nIt fills the heart with ecstasy,\n\r\nThat God, the Son of God, should take\n\r\nOur mortal form for mortals' sake."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "He sent no angel to our race\n\r\nOf higher or of lower place,\n\r\nBut wore the robe of human frame\n\r\nHimself, and to this lost world came."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "For us he was baptized, and bore\n\r\nHis holy fast, and hungered sore;\n\r\nFor us temptations sharp he knew;\n\r\nFor us the tempter overthrew."
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "For us he prayed, for us he taught,\n\r\nFor us his daily works he wrought,\n\r\nBy words, by signs, and actions, thus\n\r\nStill seeking not himself, but us."
        },
        {
          "number": 5,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "For us to wickedness betrayed,\n\r\nScourged, mocked, in purple robe arrayed,\n\r\nHe bore the shameful cross and death;\n\r\nFor us at length gave up his breath."
        },
        {
          "number": 6,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "For us he rose from death again,\n\r\nFor us he went on high to reign,\n\r\nFor us he sent his Spirit here\n\r\nTo guide, to strengthen, and to cheer."
        },
        {
          "number": 7,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "To him whose boundless love has won\n\r\nSalvation for us through his Son,\n\r\nTo God the Father, glory be\n\r\nBoth now and through eternity."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "372b",
      "title": "O Word of God Incarnate",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/372-O-Word-of-God-Incarnate.pdf",
      "notes": "Video: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uDSoNW3f9eA",
      "audioUrl": "https://hymnary.org/media/fetch/205337/public%3A//hymnary/media/ELW2006/ELW514_O_Word_of_God_Incarnate.mp3",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "O Word of God incarnate,\nO Wisdom from on high,\nO Truth, unchanged, unchanging,\nO Light of our dark sky,\nwe praise Thee for the radiance\nthat from the hallowed page,\na lantern to our footsteps,\nshines on from age to age."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "The church from her dear Master\nreceived the gift divine,\nand still that light she lifteth\no'er all the earth to shine.\nIt is the golden casket,\nwhere gems of truth are stored;\nit is the heav'n-drawn picture\nOf Christ, the living Word."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "It floateth like a banner\nbefore God's host unfurled;\nit shineth like a beacon\nabove the darkling world.\nIt is the chart and compass\nthat o'er life's surging sea,\n'mid mists and rocks and quicksands,\nstill guides, O Christ, to Thee."
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "O make Thy Church, dear Savior,\na lamp of burnished gold,\nto bear before the nations\nThy true light as of old.\nO teach Thy wand'ring pilgrims\nby this, their path to trace,\n'til, clouds and darkness ended,\nthey see Thee face to face.\nSource:\nPsalms and Hymns to the Living God #347"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "373",
      "title": "Be Thou My Vision",
      "firstLine": "Harmonized version",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/373-Be-Thou-My-Vision.pdf",
      "notes": "Harmonized version",
      "audioUrl": "https://hymnary.org/media/fetch/205832/public%3A//hymnary/media/ELW2006/ELW793_Be_Thou_My_Vision.mp3",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Be thou my vision, O Lord of my heart;\n\r\nNaught be all else to me save that thou art.\n\r\nThou my best thought by day and by night;\n\r\nWaking or sleeping, thy presence my light."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Be thou my wisdom, and thou my true Word;\n\r\nI ever with thee and thou with me, Lord.\n\r\nThou my great Father, I thy dear child;\n\r\nThou in me dwelling, with thee reconciled."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Be thou my breastplate, my sword for the fight;\n\r\nBe thou my dignity, thou my delight.\n\r\nThou my soul's shelter, thou my high tow'r;\n\r\nRaise thou me Heav'nward, O Pow'r of my pow'r."
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Riches I heed not, nor vain, empty praise;\n\r\nThou mine inheritance, now and always.\n\r\nThou and thou only, first in my heart,\n\r\nHigh King of Heaven, my treasure thou art."
        },
        {
          "number": 5,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "High King of Heaven, my victory won,\n\r\nMay I reach Heaven's joys, O bright Heav'ns Sun!\n\r\nHeart of my heart, whatever befall,\n\r\nStill be my vision, O Ruler of all."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "373 alt.",
      "title": "Be Thou My Vision (alt.)",
      "firstLine": "Unison melody with alt. harmony",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/373-alt.-Be-Thou-My-Vision.pdf",
      "audioUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Jg9IPgtGSQY&list=RD-hSD0ahDRxE&index=15",
      "notes": "Unison melody with alt. harmony\nVideo: https://youtu.be/GCrGN1zfFTE?feature=shared",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "373 alt. Be Thou My Vision\nalternate harmony"
        },
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "BeThou my vision, O Lord of my heart; Naughtbe all\nelse to me, save that Thou art— Thoumy best thought by\nday or by night, Waking or sleeping, Thy presence my light."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "374",
      "title": "Blessed Jesus, at Thy Word",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/Blessed-Jesus-at-Thy-Word.pdf",
      "audioUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-audio/Blessed-Jesus-at-Thy-Word-374.mp3",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Blessed Jesus, at your word\nwe are gathered all to hear you.\nLet our hearts and souls be stirred\nnow to seek and love and fear you.\nBy your gospel pure and holy,\nteach us, Lord, to love you solely."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "All our knowledge, sense, and sight\nlie in deepest darkness shrouded,\ntill your Spirit breaks our night\nwith your beams of truth unclouded.\nYou alone to God can win us;\nyou must work all good within us."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Glorious Lord, yourself impart;\nLight of Light, from God proceeding,\nopen lips and ears and heart;\nhelp us by your Spirit's leading.\nHear the cry your church now raises;\nLord, accept our prayers and praises."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "375",
      "title": "The Law of God is Good and Wise",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/The-Law-of-God-Is-Good-and-Wise.pdf",
      "audioUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-audio/cc_375.mp3",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Great God, indulge my heartfelt claim:\n\r\nbe now my hope, my joy, my rest;\n\r\nthe glories that compose your name\n\r\nshall all engage to make me blest.\n\r\nO great and good, O just and wise,\n\r\nmy Father, my all-loving God!\n\r\nAnd I am yours by sacred ties;\n\r\nan heir, a servant of your word.\n \nWith heart, and eyes, and lifted hands,\n\r\nI long for you, to you I look,\n\r\nas travelers, in earth’s thirsty lands,\n\r\nyearn for a cooling water-brook.\n\r\nWith eager feet I would appear\n\r\namong your saints, to seek your face;\n\r\nfor I have seen your glory there,\n\r\nand felt the power of sovereign grace.\n \nAmid the wakeful hours of night,\n\r\nwhen busy cares afflict my head,\n\r\none thought of you gives new delight,\n\r\nand adds great comfort to my bed.\n\r\nI'll lift my hands, I'll raise my voice,\n\r\nwhile I have breath to pray or praise;\n\r\nthis work shall make my heart rejoice\n\r\nfor all the hours of all my days."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "376",
      "title": "Thou Hidden Source of Calm Repose",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/Thou-Hidden-Source-of-Calm-Repose.pdf",
      "notes": "Video: https://youtu.be/On3jv8E7FEc",
      "audioUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-audio/cc_376.mp3",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Thou hidden source of calm repose,\nThou all-sufficient love divine,\nmy help and refuge from my foes,\nsecure I am, if Thou art mine;\nfrom sin and grief and shame I hide me,\nJesus, in Thy name."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Thy mighty name salvation is,\nand keeps my happy soul above;\ncomfort it brings, and pow'r and peace,\nand joy and everlasting love;\nto me, with Thy dear name, are giv'n\npardon and holiness and heav'n."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Jesus, my all in all Thou art;\nmy rest in toil, my ease in pain,\nthe healing of my broken heart,\nin war my peace, in loss my gain,\nmy smile beneath the tyrant's frown,\nin shame my glory and my crown."
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "In want my plentiful supply,\nin weakness my almighty pow'r,\nin bonds my perfect liberty,\nmy light in Satan's darkest hour,\nmy help and stay whene'er call,\nmy life in death, my heav'n, my all.\nSource:\nPsalms and Hymns to the Living God #426"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "377",
      "title": "All Praise to Thee, My God, This Night",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/All-Praise-to-Thee-My-God-This-Night.pdf",
      "audioUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-audio/cc_377.mp3",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Nearer, my God, to thee, nearer to thee!\nE'en though it be a cross that raiseth me,\nstill all my song shall be,\nnearer, my God, to thee;\nnearer, my God, to thee, nearer to thee!"
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Though like the wanderer, the sun gone down,\ndarkness be over me, my rest a stone;\nyet in my dreams I'd be\nnearer, my God, to thee;\nnearer, my God, to thee, nearer to thee!"
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "There let the way appear, steps unto heaven;\nall that thou sendest me, in mercy given;\nangels to beckon me\nnearer, my God, to thee;\nnearer, my God, to thee, nearer to thee!"
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Then, with my waking thoughts bright with thy praise,\nout of my stony griefs Bethel I'll raise;\nso by my woes to be\nnearer, my God, to thee;\nnearer, my God, to thee, nearer to thee!"
        },
        {
          "number": 5,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Or if, on joyful wing cleaving the sky,\nsun, moon, and stars forgot, upward I fly,\nstill all my song shall be,\nnearer, my God, to thee;\nnearer, my God, to thee, nearer to thee!"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "378a",
      "title": "God, That Madest Earth and Heaven",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/God-That-Madest-Earth-and-Heaven.pdf",
      "audioUrl": "https://hymnary.org/media/fetch/233375/public%3A//hymnary/media/UMH/688.mp3",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "God, who made the earth and heaven,\ndarkness and light:\nyou the day for work have given,\nfor rest the night.\nMay your angel guards defend us,\nslumber sweet your mercy send us,\nholy dreams and hopes attend us\nall through the night."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "And when morn again shall call us\nto run life's way,\nmay we still, whate'er befall us,\nyour will obey.\nFrom the pow'r of evil hide us,\nin the narrow pathway guide us,\nnever be your smile denied us\nall through the day."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Guard us waking, guard us sleeping,\nand, when we die,\nmay we in your mighty keeping\nall peaceful lie.\nWhen the last dread call shall wake us,\nthen, O Lord, do not forsake us,\nbut to reign in glory take us\nwith you on high."
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Holy Father, throned in heaven,\nall-holy Son,\nHoly Spirit, freely given,\nblest Three in One:\ngrant us grace, we now implore you,\ntill we lay our crowns before you\nand in worthier strains adore you\nwhile ages run.\nSource:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "378b",
      "title": "Love Divine, All Loves Excelling",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/Love-Divine-All-Loves-Excelling.pdf",
      "notes": "Video: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dRIFam3lDcQ&list=PLhXqXRItJDlrjAj-lIWUXf_vlOo0gwFDD&index=21",
      "audioUrl": "https://hymnary.org/media/fetch/205411/public%3A//hymnary/media/ELW2006/ELW631_Love_Divine%2C_All_Loves_Excelling.mp3",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Love divine, all loves excelling,\n\r\nJoy of Heav'n to Earth come down,\n\r\nFix in us thy humble dwelling,\n\r\nAll thy faithful mercies crown;\n\r\nJesus, thou art all compassion,\n\r\nPure, unbounded love thou art;\n\r\nVisit us with thy salvation,\n\r\nEnter ev'ry trembling heart."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Breathe, O breathe thy loving Spirit\n\r\nInto ev'ry troubled breast;\n\r\nLet us all in thee inherit,\n\r\nLet us find thy promised rest;\n\r\nTake away our love of sinning;\n\r\nAlpha and Omega be;\n\r\nEnd of faith as its beginning,\n\r\nSet our hearts at liberty."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Come, Almighty to deliver;\n\r\nLet us all thy grace receive;\n\r\nSuddenly return, and never,\n\r\nNever more thy temples leave.\n\r\nThee we would be always blessing,\n\r\nServe thee as thy host above,\n\r\nPray, and praise thee without ceasing,\n\r\nGlory in thy perfect love."
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
