      "number": "482",
      "title": "At the Lamb's High Feast We Sing",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/At-the-Lambs-High-Feast-We-Sing.pdf",
      "notes": "Video: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xdupVcUR0SE",
      "audioUrl": "https://hymnary.org/media/fetch/205246/public%3A//hymnary/media/ELW2006/ELW362_At_the_Lamb%27s_High_Feast_We_Sing.mp3",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "At the Lamb's high feast we sing\npraise to our victorious King,\nwho hath washed us in the tide\nflowing from His piercéd side;\npraise we Him whose love divine\ngives His sacred blood for wine,\ngives His body for the feast,\nChrist the Victim, Christ the Priest."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Where the paschal blood is poured,\ndeath's dark angel sheathes his sword;\nIsrael's hosts triumphant go\nthrough the wave that drowns the foe.\nPraise we Christ, whose blood was shed,\nPaschal Victim, Paschal Bread;\nwith sincerity and love\neat we manna from above."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Mighty Victim from the sky,\npow'rs of hell beneath Thee lie;\ndeath is conquered in the fight,\nThou hast brought us life and light;\nhymns of glory and of praise,\nrisen Lord, to Thee we raise;\nHoly Father, praise to Thee,\nwith the Spirit, ever be.\nSource:\nPsalms and Hymns to the Living God #382"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "484",
      "title": "Glorious Things of Thee Are Spoken",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/Glorious-Things-of-Thee-Are-Spoken.pdf",
      "notes": "Video: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pXF7SKiSCPw",
      "audioUrl": "https://hymnary.org/media/fetch/205421/public%3A//hymnary/media/ELW2006/ELW647_Glorious_Things_of_You_Are_Spoken.mp3",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Glorious things of thee are spoken,\nZion, city of our God.\nHe whose Word cannot be broken\nformed thee for His own abode.\nOn the Rock of Ages founded,\nwhat can shake thy sure repose?\nWith salvation's walls surrounded,\nthou may'st smile at all thy foes."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "See, the streams of living waters,\nspringing from eternal love,\nwell supply thy sons and daughters\nand all fear of want remove.\nWho can faint while such a river\never flows their thirst to assuage?\nGrace, which like the Lord, the Giver,\nnever fails from age to age."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "'Round each habitation hov'ring,\nsee the cloud and fire appear\nfor a glory and a cov'ring,\nshowing that the Lord is near.\nThus deriving from their banner\nlight by night and shade by day,\nsafe they feed upon the manna\nwhich He gives them on their way."
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Savior, since of Zion's city\nI through grace a member am,\nlet the world deride or pity,\nI will glory in Thy name.\nFading is the worldling's pleasures,\nall his boasted pomp and show;\nsolid joys and lasting treasures\nnone but Zion's children know.\nSource:\nPsalms and Hymns to the Living God #416"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "485",
      "title": "Hail, Thou Once-Despised Jesus",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/485-Hail-Thou-Once-Despised-Jesus.pdf",
      "audioUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-audio/Hail-Thou-Once-despised.mp3",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Hail, Thou once despised Jesus!\nHail, Thou Galilean king!\nThou didst suffer to release us;\nThou didst free salvation bring.\nHail, Thou agonizing Savior,\nbearer of our sin and shame!\nBy Thy merit we find favor;\nlife is given through Thy name."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Paschal Lamb, by God appointed,\nall our sins on Thee were laid;\nby almighty Love anointed,\nThou hast full atonement made:\nall Thy people are forgiven\nthrough the virtue of Thy blood;\nopened is the gate of heaven;\npeace is made 'twixt man and God."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Jesus, hail, enthroned in glory,\nthere forever to abide!\nAll the heav'nly host adore Thee,\nseated at Thy Father's side.\nThere for sinners Thou art pleading;\nthere Thou dost our place prepare;\never for us interceding,\ntill in glory we appear."
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Worship, honor, pow'r, and blessing\nThou art worthy to receive;\nhighest praises, without ceasing,\nmeet it is for us to give.\nHelp, ye bright angelic spirits,\nbring your sweetest, noblest lays;\nhelp to sing our Savior's merits;\nhelp to chant Immanuel's praise!\nSource:\nPsalms and Hymns to the Living God #297"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "488",
      "title": "My Song Is Love Unkown",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/488-My-Song-Is-Love-Unknown.pdf",
      "notes": "Video: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Cdq0dXrWgkk",
      "audioUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-audio/cc_488.mp3",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Bless'd be the Father and his love,\nTo whose celestial source we owe\nRivers of endless joy above,\nAnd rills of comfort here below."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Glory to thee, great Son of God,\nFrom whose dear wounded body rolls\nA precious stream of vital blood,\nPardon and life for dying souls."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "We give thee, sacred Spirit, praise,\nWho in our hearts of sin and woe\nMakes living springs of grace arise,\nAnd into boundless glory flow."
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Thus God the Father, God the Son,\nAnd God the Spirit we adore;\nThat sea of life and love unknown,\nWithout a bottom or a shore.\nSource:\nA Selection of Hymns for Public Worship. In four parts (10th ed.) (Gadsby's Hymns) #33"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "491",
      "title": "Only-Begotten, Word of God Eternal",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/Only-Begotten-Word-of-God-Eternal.pdf",
      "notes": "Video: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZHVNjTgY1r0",
      "audioUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-audio/cc_491.mid",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Only-begotten, Word of God eternal,\nLord of creation, merciful and mighty,\nHear us, your servants, when our tuneful voices\nRise to your presence."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Holy this dwelling where the Lord is present;\nThis is none other than the gate of heaven;\nStrangers and pilgrims, seeking homes eternal,\nPass through its portals."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Lord, we beseech you, as we throng your temple,\nBy your past blessings, by your present bounty,\nSmile on your children, and with tender mercy\nHear our petitions."
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "God in three Persons, Father everlasting,\nSon co-eternal, ever blessed Spirit,\nYours be the glory, praise and adoration,\nNow and forever.\nSource:\nWorship (4th ed.) #839"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "494",
      "title": "Jesus Christ, Our Blessed Savior",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/Jesus-Christ-Our-Blessed-Savior.pdf",
      "audioUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-audio/Jesus-Christ-Our-Blessed.mp3",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Savior, like a shepherd lead us,\nMuch we need Thy tender care;\nIn Thy pleasant pastures feed us,\nFor our use Thy folds prepare:\nBlessèd Jesus, blessèd Jesus,\nThou hast bought us, Thine we are;\nBlessèd Jesus, blessèd Jesus,\nThou hast bought us, Thine we are."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "We are Thine, do Thou befriend us,\nBe the guardian of our way;\nKeep Thy flock, from sin defend us,\nSeek us when we go astray:\nBlessèd Jesus, blessèd Jesus,\nHear, O hear us when we pray;\nBlessèd Jesus, blessèd Jesus,\nHear, O hear us when we pray."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Thou hast promised to receive us,\nPoor and sinful though we be;\nThou hast mercy to relieve us,\nGrace to cleanse, and pow'r to free:\nBlessèd Jesus, blessèd Jesus,\nEarly let us turn to Thee;\nBlessèd Jesus, blessèd Jesus,\nEarly let us turn to Thee."
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Early let us seek Thy favor,\nEarly let us do Thy will;\nBlessed Lord and only Savior,\nWith Thy love our bosoms fill:\nBlessèd Jesus, blessèd Jesus,\nThou hast loved us, love us still;\nBlessèd Jesus, blessèd Jesus,\nThou hast loved us, love us still.\nHymns for the Living Church"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "498",
      "title": "Author of Life Divine",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/Author-of-Life-Divine.pdf",
      "audioUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-audio/Author-of-Life.mp3",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Love divine, all loves excelling,\n\r\nJoy of Heav'n to Earth come down,\n\r\nFix in us thy humble dwelling,\n\r\nAll thy faithful mercies crown;\n\r\nJesus, thou art all compassion,\n\r\nPure, unbounded love thou art;\n\r\nVisit us with thy salvation,\n\r\nEnter ev'ry trembling heart."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Breathe, O breathe thy loving Spirit\n\r\nInto ev'ry troubled breast;\n\r\nLet us all in thee inherit,\n\r\nLet us find thy promised rest;\n\r\nTake away our love of sinning;\n\r\nAlpha and Omega be;\n\r\nEnd of faith as its beginning,\n\r\nSet our hearts at liberty."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Come, Almighty to deliver;\n\r\nLet us all thy grace receive;\n\r\nSuddenly return, and never,\n\r\nNever more thy temples leave.\n\r\nThee we would be always blessing,\n\r\nServe thee as thy host above,\n\r\nPray, and praise thee without ceasing,\n\r\nGlory in thy perfect love."
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Finish, then, thy new creation;\n\r\nPure and spotless let us be;\n\r\nLet us see thy great salvation\n\r\nPerfectly restored in thee;\n\r\nChanged from glory into glory\n\r\nTill in Heav'n we take our place,\n\r\nTill we cast our crowns before thee,\n\r\nLost in wonder, love, and praise!"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "499",
      "title": "How Sweet and Awful Is the Place",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/How-Sweet-and-Awful-Is-the-Place.pdf",
      "notes": "Video: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lKrek6b0_p4",
      "audioUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-audio/cc_499.mid",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "How sweet and awful is the place\nwith Christ within the doors,\nwhile everlasting love displays\nthe choicest of her stores."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "While all our hearts and all our songs\njoin to admire the feast,\neach of us cries, with thankful tongue,\n\"Lord, why was I a guest?"
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "\"Why was I made to hear Thy voice,\nand enter while there's room,\nwhen thousands make a wretched choice\nand rather starve than come?\""
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "'Twas the same love that spread the feast\nthat sweetly drew us in;\nelse we had still refused to taste,\nand perished in our sin."
        },
        {
          "number": 5,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Pity the nations, O our God,\nconstrain the earth to come;\nsend Thy victorious Word abroad,\nand bring the strangers home."
        },
        {
          "number": 6,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "We long to see Thy churches full,\nthat all the chosen race\nmay, with one voice and heart and soul,\nsing Thy redeeming grace.\nSource:\nPsalms and Hymns to the Living God #312"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "504",
      "title": "Jesus, Thy Blood and Righteousness",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/Jesus-They-Blood-and-Righteousness.pdf",
      "notes": "Video: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dtpwuUuDB2s",
      "audioUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-audio/cc_504.mid",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Jesus, thy blood and righteousness,\n\r\nMy beauty are, my glorious dress;\n\r\nMidst flaming worlds, in these arrayed,\n\r\nWith joy shall I lift up my head."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "The holy, meek, unspotted Lamb,\n\r\nWho from the Father's bosom came,\n\r\nWho died for me, e'en me t' atone,\n\r\nNow for my Lord and God I own."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Lord, I believe thy precious blood,\n\r\nWhich at the mercy seat of God,\n\r\nForever doth for sinners plead,\n\r\nFor me, e'en for my soul was shed."
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "When from the dust of death I rise\n\r\nTo claim my mansion in the skies,\n\r\nE’en then this shall be all my plea,\n\r\nJesus hath lived, hath died for me."
        },
        {
          "number": 5,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Jesus, be endless praise to thee,\n\r\nWhose boundless mercy hath for me\n\r\nAnd all who trust thy hands hath made\n\r\nAn everlasting ransom paid."
        },
        {
          "number": 6,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Ah! give to all, almighty Lord,\n\r\nWith pow’r to speak thy gracious word,\n\r\nThat all who to thy wounds will flee\n\r\nMay find eternal life in thee."
        },
        {
          "number": 7,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Oh, let the dead now hear thy voice!\n\r\nNow bid thy banished ones rejoice;\n\r\nTheir beauty this, their glorious dress,\n\r\nJesus, thy blood and righteousness."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "510",
      "title": "Who Would True Valor See",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/510-Who-Would-True-Valor-See.pdf",
      "notes": "Video: https://youtu.be/HGjvlR-9NbQ?feature=shared",
      "audioUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-audio/cc_510.mid",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "All who would valiant be\n\r\n'Gainst all disaster,\n\r\nLet them in constancy\n\r\nFollow the master.\n\r\nThere's no discouragement\n\r\nShall make them once relent\n\r\nTheir first avowed intent\n\r\nTo be true pilgrims."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Who so beset them round\n\r\nWith dismal stories,\n\r\nDo but themselves confound;\n\r\nTheir strength the more is.\n\r\nNo foes shall stay their might;\n\r\nThough they with giants fight,\n\r\nThey will make good their right\n\r\nTo be true pilgrims."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Since, Lord, you will defend\n\r\nUs with your Spirit,\n\r\nWe know we at the end\n\r\nShall life inherit.\n\r\nThen fancies flee away!\n\r\nWe'll fear not what they say,\n\r\nWe'll labor night and day\n\r\nTo be true pilgrims."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "518",
      "title": "I Bind unto Myself Today",
      "firstLine": "Saint Patrick's Breastplate",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/I-bind-unto-Myself-Today.pdf",
      "audioUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-audio/St.-Patricks-Breastplate.mp3",
      "notes": "Saint Patrick's Breastplate\nVideo: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OS8lm5Cx7xU",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "I bind unto myself today\nthe strong name of the Trinity,\nby invocation of the same,\nthe Three in One, and One in Three."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "I bind unto myself today\nthe virtues of the star-lit heaven,\nthe glorious sun's life-giving ray,\nthe whiteness of the moon at even,\nthe flashing of the lightning free,\nthe whirling wind's tempestuous shocks,\nthe stable earth, the deep salt sea\naround the old eternal rocks."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "I bind unto myself today\nthe power of God to hold and lead,\nhis eye to watch, his might to stay,\nhis ear to hearken to my need;\nthe wisdom of my God to teach,\nhis hand to guide, his shield to ward,\nthe word of God to give me speech,\nhis heavenly host to be my guard."
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "I bind unto myself the name,\nthe strong name of the Trinity,\nby invocation of the same,\nthe Three in One, and One in Three,\nof whom all nature hath creation,\neternal Father, Spirit, Word.\nPraise to the Lord of my salvation:\nsalvation is of Christ the Lord.\nSource:\nAncient and Modern: hymns and songs for refreshing worship #277a"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "521",
      "title": "Lead On, O King Eternal",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/Lead-On-O-King-Eternal.pdf",
      "notes": "Video: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sQPHbe_RKuM",
      "audioUrl": "https://hymnary.org/media/fetch/205840/public%3A//hymnary/media/ELW2006/ELW805_Lead_On%2C_O_King_Eternal%21.mp3",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Lead on, O King eternal,\nthe day of march has come;\nhenceforth in fields of conquest\nyour tents will be our home.\nThrough days of preparation\nyour grace has made us strong;\nand now, O King eternal,\nwe lift our battle song."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Lead on, O King eternal,\ntill sin's fierce war shall cease,\nand holiness shall whisper\nthe sweet amen of peace.\nFor not with swords' loud clashing\nor roll of stirring drums\nwith deeds of love and mercy\nthe heavenly kingdom comes."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Lead on, O King eternal;\nwe follow, not with fears,\nfor gladness breaks like morning\nwhere'er your face appears.\nYour cross is lifted o'er us,\nwe journey in its light;\nthe crown awaits the conquest;\nlead on, O God of might."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "522",
      "title": "Lo! He Comes",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/522-Lo-He-Comes.pdf",
      "audioUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-audio/Lo-He-Comes-522.mp3",
      "notes": "Video: https://youtu.be/oTJaHAPEQ0g",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "1. Lo! he comes with clouds descending,\n\r\nOnce for favored sinners slain!\n\r\nThousand, thousand saints attending,\n\r\nSwell the triumph of his train.\n\r\nAlleluia!\n\r\nAlleluia!\n\r\nAlleluia!\n\r\nGod appears on Earth to reign."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "2. Ev'ry eye shall now behold him,\n\r\nRobed in dreadful majesty;\n\r\nThose who set at naught and sold him,\n\r\nPierced and nailed him to a tree,\n\r\nDeeply wailing,\n\r\nDeeply wailing,\n\r\nDeeply wailing,\n\r\nShall the true Messiah see."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "3. The dear tokens of his passion\n\r\nStill his dazzling body bears,\n\r\nCause of endless exultation\n\r\nTo his ransomed worshipers;\n\r\nWith what rapture,\n\r\nWith what rapture,\n\r\nWith what rapture\n\r\nGaze we on those glorious scars."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "527",
      "title": "When the Enemy Comes In",
      "firstLine": "Wessex Battle Song",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/527-When-the-Enemy-Comes-In.pdf",
      "audioUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-audio/When-the-Enemy-Comes-In-Wessex-Battle-Song-527.mp3",
      "notes": "Wessex Battle Song",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "When the storms of life are raging,\nTempests wild on sea and land,\nI will seek a place of refuge\nIn the shadow of God’s hand."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": true,
          "text": "He will hide me, He will hide me,\nWhere no harm can e’er betide me;\nHe will hide me, safely hide me,\nIn the shadow of His hand."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Though He may send some affliction,\n’Twill but make me long for home;\nFor in love and not in anger,\nAll His chastenings will come. [Refrain]"
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Enemies may strive to injure,\nSatan all his arts employ;\nHe will turn what seems to harm me\nInto everlasting joy. [Refrain]"
        },
        {
          "number": 5,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "So while here the cross I’m bearing,\nMeeting storms and billows wild,\nJesus for my soul is caring,\nNaught can harm His Father’s child. [Refrain]\nEvening Light Songs, 1987 (Timeless Truths)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "528",
      "title": "Shout, For the Blessed Jesus Reigns",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/528-Shout-for-the-Blessed-Jesus-Reigns.pdf",
      "audioUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-audio/Shout-for-the-Blessed.mp3",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Shout, for the blessed Jesus reigns;\nthrough distant lands his triumphs spread;\nand sinners, freed from endless pains,\nown him their Savior and their Head."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "He calls his chosen from afar;\nthey all at Zion's gates arrive;\nthose who were dead in sin before\nby sov'reign grace are made alive."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Gentiles and Jews his laws obey;\nnations remote their off'rings bring,\nand unconstrained their homage pay\nto their exalted God and King."
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "O may his holy church increase,\nhis Word and Spirit still prevail,\nwhile angels celebrate his praise,\nand saints his growing glories hail."
        },
        {
          "number": 5,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Loud hallelujahs to the Lamb,\nfrom all below and all above!\nIn lofty songs exalt his name,\nin songs as lasting as his love.\nSource:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "529",
      "title": "See the Conqueror Mounts in Triumph",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/See-the-Conqueror-Mounts-in-Triumph.pdf",
      "notes": "Video: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Q-IvYjZB9IQ",
      "audioUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-audio/cc_529.mid",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "See, the conq'ror mounts in triumph,\n\r\nSee the King in royal state,\n\r\nRiding on the clouds, his chariot,\n\r\nTo his heav'nly palace gate;\n\r\nHark, the choirs of angel voices\n\r\nJoyful hallelujahs sing,\n\r\nAnd the portals high and lifted\n\r\nTo receive their heav'nly King."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Who is this who comes in glory,\n\r\nWith the trump of jubilee?\n\r\nLord of battles, God of armies,\n\r\nHe has gained the victory;\n\r\nHe who on the cross did suffer,\n\r\nHe who from the grave arose,\n\r\nHe has vanquished sin and Satan,\n\r\nHe by death has spoiled his foes."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "While he raised his hands in blessing,\n\r\nHe was parted from his friends;\n\r\nWhile his eager eyes behold him,\n\r\nHe upon the clouds ascends;\n\r\nHe who walked with God and pleased him,\n\r\nPreaching truth and doom to come,\n\r\nChrist, our Enoch, is translated\n\r\nTo his everlasting home."
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Raise us from the Earth to Heaven,\n\r\nGive us wings of faith and love,\n\r\nGales of holy aspirations\n\r\nWafting us to realms above;\n\r\nThat with hearts and minds uplifted,\n\r\nWe with Christ our Lord may dwell,\n\r\nWhere he sits enthroned in glory,\n\r\nIn his heav'nly citadel."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
