          "text": "O wondrous type! O vision fair\nof glory that the Church may share,\nwhich Christ upon the mountain shows,\nwhere brighter than the sun he glows!"
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "With Moses and Elijah nigh\nth'incarnate Lord holds converse high,\nand from the cloud the Holy One\nbears record to the only Son."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "With shining face and bright array\nChrist deigns to manifest today\nwhat glory shall be theirs above\nwho joy in God with perfect love."
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "And faithful hearts are raised on high\nby this great vision's mystery,\nfor which in joyful strains we raise\nthe voice of prayer, the hymn of praise."
        },
        {
          "number": 5,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "O Father, with th'eternal Son\nand Holy Spirit ever one,\nwe pray you, bring us by your grace\nto see your glory face to face.\nSource:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "611",
      "title": "O Love, How Deep, How Broad, How High!",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/611-O-Love-How-Deep-How-Broad-How-High.pdf",
      "notes": "Video: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9cYmfPJz5kE",
      "audioUrl": "https://hymnary.org/media/fetch/205223/public%3A//hymnary/media/ELW2006/ELW322_Oh%2C_Love%2C_How_Deep.mp3",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "O love, how deep, how broad, how high!\n\r\nIt fills the heart with ecstasy,\n\r\nThat God, the Son of God, should take\n\r\nOur mortal form for mortals' sake."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "He sent no angel to our race\n\r\nOf higher or of lower place,\n\r\nBut wore the robe of human frame\n\r\nHimself, and to this lost world came."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "For us he was baptized, and bore\n\r\nHis holy fast, and hungered sore;\n\r\nFor us temptations sharp he knew;\n\r\nFor us the tempter overthrew."
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "For us he prayed, for us he taught,\n\r\nFor us his daily works he wrought,\n\r\nBy words, by signs, and actions, thus\n\r\nStill seeking not himself, but us."
        },
        {
          "number": 5,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "For us to wickedness betrayed,\n\r\nScourged, mocked, in purple robe arrayed,\n\r\nHe bore the shameful cross and death;\n\r\nFor us at length gave up his breath."
        },
        {
          "number": 6,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "For us he rose from death again,\n\r\nFor us he went on high to reign,\n\r\nFor us he sent his Spirit here\n\r\nTo guide, to strengthen, and to cheer."
        },
        {
          "number": 7,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "To him whose boundless love has won\n\r\nSalvation for us through his Son,\n\r\nTo God the Father, glory be\n\r\nBoth now and through eternity."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "613",
      "title": "Ride On, Ride On in Majesty",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/613-Ride-On-Ride-On-in-Majesty.pdf",
      "notes": "Video: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VAh1lzSQ3P4",
      "audioUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-audio/cc_613.mp3",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Ride on, ride on in majesty!\nHear all the tribes hosanna cry;\nO Savior meek, pursue Your road\nwith palms and scattered garments strowed."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Ride on, ride on in majesty!\nIn lowly pomp ride on to die.\nO Christ, Your triumphs now begin\no’er captive death and conquered sin."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Ride on, ride on in majesty!\nThe host of angels in the sky\nlook down with sad and wond'ring eyes\nto see th'approaching Sacrifice."
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Ride on, ride on in majesty!\nYour last and fiercest strife is nigh.\nThe Father on His sapphire throne\nawaits His own anointed Son."
        },
        {
          "number": 5,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Ride on, ride on in majesty!\nIn lowly pomp ride on to die,\nbow Your meek head to mortal pain,\nthen take, O Christ, Your pow'r and reign.\nSource:\nPsalms and Hymns to the Living God #259"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "620",
      "title": "Stricken Smitten and Afflicted",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/Stricken-Smitten-and-Afflicted.pdf",
      "notes": "Video: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=T8bshWdiCDA",
      "audioUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-audio/cc_620.mp3",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "1. Stricken, smitten and afflicted,\n\r\nSee him dying on the tree!\n\r\n'Tis the Christ by man rejected!\n\r\nYes, my soul, 'tis he! 'tis he!\n\r\n'Tis the long-expected prophet,\n\r\nDavid's son, yet David's Lord;\n\r\nProofs I see sufficient of it:\n\r\n'Tis a true and faithful word."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "2. Tell me, ye who hear him groaning,\n\r\nWas there ever grief like his?\n\r\nFriends thru' fear His cause disowning,\n\r\nFoes insulting his distress:\n\r\nMany hands were raised to wound him,\n\r\nNone would interpose to save;\n\r\nBut the awful stroke that pierced him\n\r\nWas the stroke that justice gave."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "3. Ye who think of sin but lightly,\n\r\nNor suppose the evil great;\n\r\nHere may view its nature rightly,\n\r\nHere its guilt may estimate.\n\r\nMark the sacrifice appointed!\n\r\nSee who bears the awful load!\n\r\n'Tis the Word, the Lord's anointed,\n\r\nSon of man, and Son of God."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "622",
      "title": "Man of Sorrows! What a Name",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/622-Man-of-Sorrows-What-a-Name.pdf",
      "notes": "Video: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uOOncVlwKIU&list=RD-hSD0ahDRxE&index=33",
      "audioUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-audio/cc_622.mp3",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Man of sorrows what a name\nfor the Son of God, who came\nruined sinners to reclaim:\nHallelujah, what a Savior!"
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Bearing shame and scoffing rude,\nin my place condemned he stood,\nsealed my pardon with his blood:\nHallelujah, what a Savior!"
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Guilty, helpless, lost were we;\nblameless Lamb of God was he,\nsacrificed to set us free:\nHallelujah, what a Savior!"
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "He was lifted up to die;\n\"It is finished\" was his cry;\nnow in heaven exalted high:\nHallelujah, what a Savior!"
        },
        {
          "number": 5,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "When he comes, our glorious King,\nall his ransomed home to bring,\nthen anew this song we'll sing:\nHallelujah, what a Savior!"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "626",
      "title": "When I Survey the Wondrous Cross",
      "firstLine": "Lyrics: Isaac Watts 1707 Music: Lowell Mason 1824",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/When-I-Survey-the-Wondrous-Cross.pdf",
      "notes": "Lyrics: Isaac Watts 1707 Music: Lowell Mason 1824\nVideo: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9wxFQCvv1uk",
      "audioUrl": "https://hymnary.org/media/fetch/205839/public%3A//hymnary/media/ELW2006/ELW803_When_I_Survey_the_Wondrous_Cross.mp3",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "When I survey the wondrous cross\non which the Prince of glory died,\nmy richest gain I count but loss,\nand pour contempt on all my pride."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Forbid it, Lord, that I should boast\nsave in the death of Christ, my God!\nAll the vain things that charm me most,\nI sacrifice them through his blood."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "See, from his head, his hands, his feet,\nsorrow and love flow mingled down.\nDid e'er such love and sorrow meet,\nor thorns compose so rich a crown?"
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Were the whole realm of nature mine,\nthat were a present far too small.\nLove so amazing, so divine,\ndemands my soul, my life, my all."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "627",
      "title": "That Easter Day with Joy was Bright",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/That-Easter-Day-with-Joy-was-Bright.pdf",
      "notes": "Video: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sSw_bj3KbEk",
      "audioUrl": "https://hymnary.org/media/fetch/205263/public%3A//hymnary/media/ELW2006/ELW384_That_Easter_Day_with_Joy_Was_Bright.mp3",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "That Easter day with joy was bright:\nThe sun shone out with fairer light\nWhen, to their longing eyes restored,\nThe_apostles saw their risen Lord!"
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "His risen flesh with radiance glowed;\nHis wounded hands and feet He showed;\nThose scars their solemn witness gave\nThat Christ was risen from the grave."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "O Jesus, King of gentleness,\nWith constant love our hearts possess\nThat we may give You all our days\nThe tribute of our grateful praise."
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "O Lord of all, with us abide\nIn this our joyful Eastertide;\nFrom ev’ry weapon death can wield\nYour own redeemed forever shield."
        },
        {
          "number": 5,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "All praise to you, O risen Lord,\nNow both by heav’n and earth adored;\nTo God the Father equal praise,\nAnd God the Spirit, now we raise!\nSource:\nOne and All Rejoice #221"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "629",
      "title": "Christ Jesus Lay in Death's Strong Bands",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/Christ-Jesus-Lay-in-Deaths-Storng-Bands.pdf",
      "audioUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-audio/Christ-Jesus-Lay-in-Deaths-Strong-Bands.mp3",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Christ Jesus lay in death’s strong bands,\nfor our offenses given;\nbut now at God’s right hand He stands\nand brings us light from heaven.\nTherefore let us joyful be\nand sing to God right thankfully\nloud songs of hallelujah.\nHallelujah!"
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "It was a strange and dreadful strife\nwhen life and death contended;\nthe victory remained with life,\nthe reign of death was ended.\nHoly Scripture plainly saith\nthat death is swallowed up by death;\nhis sting is lost forever.\nHallelujah!"
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Here the true Paschal Lamb we see,\nwhom God so freely gave us;\nHe died on the accursed tree-\nso strong His love to save us.\nSee His blood upon our door;\nfaith points to it, death passes o'er,\nand Satan cannot harm us.\nHallelujah!"
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "So let us keep the festival\nwhereto the Lord invites us;\nChrist is Himself the Joy of all,\nthe Sun that warms and lights us.\nBy His grace He doth impart\neternal sunshine to the heart;\nthe night of sin is ended.\nHallelujah!\nSource:\nPsalms and Hymns to the Living God #292"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "631",
      "title": "Christ the Lord is Risen Today",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/Christ-the-Lord-is-Risen-Today.pdf",
      "notes": "Video: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-hSD0ahDRxE&list=RD-hSD0ahDRxE&index=1",
      "audioUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-audio/cc_631.mp3",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Christ the Lord is risen today, Alleluia!\nEarth and heaven in chorus say, Alleluia!\nRaise your joys and triumphs high, Alleluia!\nSing, ye heavens, and earth reply, Alleluia!"
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Love's redeeming work is done, Alleluia!\nFought the fight, the battle won, Alleluia!\nDeath in vain forbids him rise, Alleluia!\nChrist has opened paradise, Alleluia!"
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Lives again our glorious King, Alleluia!\nWhere, O death, is now thy sting? Alleluia!\nOnce he died our souls to save, Alleluia!\nWhere's thy victory, boasting grave? Alleluia!"
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Soar we now where Christ has led, Alleluia!\nFollowing our exalted Head, Alleluia!\nMade like him, like him we rise, Alleluia!\nOurs the cross, the grave, the skies, Alleluia!"
        },
        {
          "number": 5,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Hail the Lord of earth and heaven, Alleluia!\nPraise to thee by both be given, Alleluia!\nThee we greet triumphant now, Alleluia!\nHail the Resurrection, thou, Alleluia!"
        },
        {
          "number": 6,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "King of glory, soul of bliss, Alleluia!\nEverlasting life is this, Alleluia!\nThee to know, thy power to prove, Alleluia!\nThus to sing, and thus to love, Alleluia!"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "635",
      "title": "Now Let the Vault of Heaven Resound",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/635-Now-Let-the-Vault-of-Heaven-Resound.pdf",
      "notes": "Video: https://youtu.be/If_4PFYhYO0?si=-iDueQgjRkVxq6YC",
      "audioUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-audio/cc_635.mp3",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Seek the Lord who now is present, pray to One who is at hand.\nLet the wicked cease from sinning, evildoers change their mind.\nOn the sinful God has pity; those returning God forgives.\nThis is what the Lord is saying to a world that disbelieves."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "“Judge Me not by human standards! As the vault of heaven soars\nHigh above the earth, so higher are my thoughts and ways than yours.\nSee how rain and snow from heaven make earth blossom and bear fruit,\nGiving you, before returning, seed for sowing, bread to eat:"
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "“So My Word returns not fruitless; does not from its labors cease\nTill it has achieved My purpose in a world of joy and peace.”\nGod is love! How close the prophet to that vital gospel word!\nIn Isaiah’s inspiration it is Jesus we have heard!"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "646",
      "title": "Christ is Risen, Christ Ascended",
      "firstLine": "Ode to Joy",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/646-Christ-Is-Risen-Christ-Ascended.pdf",
      "audioUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-audio/Christ-is-Risen-Christ-Ascended.mp3",
      "notes": "Ode to Joy",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Christ the Lord is ris'n again;\nChrist has broken death's strong chain.\nHark, the angels shout for joy,\nsinging evermore on high:\nHallelujah!"
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "He who gave for us his life,\nwho for us endured the strife,\nis our Paschal Lamb today.\nWe too sing for joy and say:\nHallelujah!"
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "He who bore all pain and loss\ncomfortless upon the cross\nlives in glory now on high,\npleads for us, and hears our cry:\nHallelujah!"
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "He whose path no records tell\nhas descended into hell;\nhe the strong man armed has bound\nand in highest heav'n is crowned.\nHallelujah!"
        },
        {
          "number": 5,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "He who slumbered in the grave\nis exalted now to save;\nnow through Christendom it rings\nthat the Lamb is King of kings.\nHallelujah!"
        },
        {
          "number": 6,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Now he bids us tell abroad\nhow the lost may be restored,\nhow the penitent forgiv'n,\nhow we too may enter heav'n,\nHallelujah!\nSource:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "650",
      "title": "Come, Holy Ghost, Our Souls Inspire",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/Come-Holy-Ghost-Our-Souls-Inspire.pdf",
      "audioUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-audio/Come-Holy-Ghost-Our-Souls-Inspire-650.mp3",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Come, Holy Ghost, our souls inspire,\nand lighten with celestial fire;\nthou the anointing Spirit art,\nwho dost thy sevenfold gifts impart:"
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Thy blessèd unction from above\nis comfort, life, and fire of love;\nenable with perpetual light\nthe dullness of our blinded sight:"
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Anoint and cheer our soiled face\nwith the abundance of thy grace:\nkeep far our foes, give peace at home;\nwhere thou art guide no ill can come."
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Teach us to know the Father, Son,\nand thee, of both, to be but One;\nthat through the ages all along\nthis may be our endless song,"
        },
        {
          "number": 5,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Praise to thy eternal merit,\nFather, Son, and Holy Spirit. Amen.\nSource:\nAncient and Modern: hymns and songs for refreshing worship #241"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "656",
      "title": "The Sword of the Spirit",
      "firstLine": "Tallis Canon",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/656-The-Sword-of-the-Spirit.pdf",
      "audioUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-audio/The-Sword-of-the-Spirit.mp3",
      "notes": "Tallis Canon",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Come, O come, life-giving Spirit,\nGod from all eternity!\nMay your power never fail us;\ndwell within us constantly.\nThen shall truth and life and light\nbanish all the gloom of night."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Show us, Lord, the path of blessing;\nwhen we trespass on our way,\ncast, O Lord, our sins behind you\nand be with us day by day.\nShould we stray, O Lord, recall;\nwork repentance when we fall."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Spirit, guard our faith forever;\nlet not Satan, death, or shame\never part us from our Savior.\nLord, our refuge is your name!\nWhen our hearts oppose your will,\nlet your Word prove stronger still."
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "And when life's frail thread is breaking,\nthen assure us more and more,\nas the heirs of life unending,\nof the glory there in store,\nglory never yet expressed,\nglory of the saints at rest.\nSource:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "662",
      "title": "Come Down, O Love Divine",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/Come-Down-O-Love-Divine.pdf",
      "notes": "Video: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6HPKL1wOVXk",
      "audioUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-audio/cc_662.mp3",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Come down, O Love divine, \n\r\nseek thou this soul of mine, \n\r\nand visit it with thine own ardor glowing; \n\r\nO Comforter, draw near, \n\r\nwithin my heart appear, \n\r\nand kindle it, thy holy flame bestowing."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "O let it freely burn, \n\r\ntill earthly passions turn \n\r\nto dust and ashes in its heat consuming; \n\r\nand let thy glorious light \n\r\nshine ever on my sight, \n\r\nand clothe me round, the while my path illuming."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "And so the yearning strong, \n\r\nwith which the soul will long, \n\r\nshall far outpass the power of human telling; \n\r\nfor none can guess its grace, \n\r\ntill Love create a place \n\r\nwherein the Holy Spirit makes a dwelling.\n \nUnited Methodist Hymnal, 1989"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "663",
      "title": "The Church's One Foundation",
      "sheetMusicUrl": "/hymnal-media/cc-sheet/The-Churchs-One-Foundation.pdf",
      "notes": "Video: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1ooRvCyULoU",
      "audioUrl": "https://hymnary.org/media/fetch/205764/public%3A//hymnary/media/ELW2006/ELW654_The_Church%27s_One_Foundation.mp3",
      "verses": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "The Church's one foundation\n\r\nIs Jesus Christ her Lord;\n\r\nShe is his new creation,\n\r\nBy water and the word;\n\r\nFrom Heav'n he came and sought her\n\r\nTo be his holy bride;\n\r\nWith his own blood he bought her,\n\r\nAnd for her life he died."
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "Elect from ev'ry nation,\n\r\nYet one o'er all the Earth,\n\r\nHer charter of salvation\n\r\nOne Lord, one faith, one birth;\n\r\nOne holy name she blesses,\n\r\nPartakes one holy food,\n\r\nAnd to one hope she presses,\n\r\nWith ev'ry grace endued."
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "'Mid toil and tribulation\n\r\nAnd tumult of her war,\n\r\nShe waits the consummation\n\r\nOf peace forever more;\n\r\nTill with the vision glorious\n\r\nHer longing eyes are blest,\n\r\nAnd the great Church victorious\n\r\nShall be the Church at rest."
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "isChorus": false,
          "text": "O happy ones and holy!\n\r\nLord, give us grace that we\n\r\nLike them, the meek and lowly,\n\r\nOn high may dwell with thee;\n\r\nThere, past the border mountains,\n\r\nWhere in sweet vales, the bride\n\r\nWith thee, by living fountains,\n\r\nForever shall abide!"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "665",
